failure rules in force:
  - A posim fragment FAILS if the process exits nonzero.
  - A posim fragment FAILS if stdout contains any line starting `Err[`.
  - A posim fragment FAILS if stdout contains a line matching `^%\w+ .* failed:` — a failing magic (notably %load) exits 0 and emits NO Err[ line, so exit status alone would pass it vacuously.
  - posim fragments must be run with cwd = the repository root: %load and %save resolve paths relative to the current directory.
  - POSIM_NO_BROWSER=1 must be set so SCENE CREATE does not launch a browser.
  - Captured output has run-to-run variation normalised: the OS-assigned scene port becomes <port>, and the playback step and history counters become <varies> because playback advances on wall-clock time. Solver step counts are NOT normalised — those are deterministic, and they are the anchors the documentation pins.

